 r"I am writing to apply for the Trading Performance Analyst position for Hospitals and Primary Care at Nuffield Health. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have tracked performance against KPIs, explained what is driving the numbers, and turned that into recommendations that operational and commercial teams act on.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the analysis has a visible end point: hospital and primary care services that run more efficiently and give patients faster access to treatment, which in turn supports Nuffield Health's purpose as a charity. The posting describes analysing enquiry conversion, referral-to-treatment times and clinical activity, producing weekly performance packs and explaining performance to operational and executive teams, which combines the two areas I know best: performance analytics and healthcare data. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse large merchant and transaction datasets in SQL and Python to find the drivers behind over- and under-performance across the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Much of the job is explaining why a number has moved to people who do not work with data every day, and the recurring lesson has been that the first metric someone asks for is rarely the one that answers their question. I also used Claude Code to automate a repetitive campaign configuration task, which cut the time it took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"My healthcare background is where this role fits most naturally. My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants to model cardiovascular risk, which taught me how clinical activity and outcomes are recorded and how easily they can be misread. At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing service for a pharmaceutical client, turning more than 4,800 patient consultation threads into structured data and presenting findings to clinical and business stakeholders. Both taught me to check that a healthcare metric means what people think it means before acting on it.",

